== 5. What step 2 can answer ===================================
  The expression gate (42, 43) returned STOP: RASSF9 is at the detection
  floor in melanoma lines, so no methylation-expression CORRELATION is
  computable. 44b therefore does not attempt one.

  It answers the one question that survives zero expression variance:
  is the RASSF9 promoter core METHYLATED in melanoma cells?

    high in lines  -> silencing consistent with the TCGA direction; the
                      correlation is untestable in lines only because the
                      gene is uniformly off
    low in lines   -> methylation is not what holds RASSF9 off in
                      melanoma cells, and the TCGA association is more
                      likely driven by the non-malignant compartments
                      where the gene is actually expressed

  The shore and distal probes are carried through as internal controls,
  and the TCGA median for each probe travels in the probe table so the
  two can be put side by side per probe rather than as pooled averages.

  WHAT NEITHER SCRIPT CAN SAY: cell lines are not tumours. Cultured lines
  drift epigenetically, and a difference from TCGA may reflect culture
  rather than malignant-cell biology in vivo. This is a supporting
  observation, not a test of the TCGA finding.
